What was adapted, and how. All of it was rewritten for presentation slides; no file
was copied verbatim.

- Direction flow (new-work.md, shape.md, init.md): the question round, scene
  sentence, the audience's visual world, directions, the direction contract, the
  finish with bounded passes, fresh review and dispositions. Rendered draft slides
  replace Impeccable's browser comps. -> references/direction.md, references/deck-plan.md
- Quality floor and refuse list (craft-floor.md), including the four default looks
  and the calibration against them. -> references/refuse.md, references/rules-core.md
- Mode names and their intent (audit, critique, polish, distill, typeset, layout,
  clarify, bolder, quieter). -> references/commands.md
- Deterministic detector rules (crates/live/assets/antipatterns.json), transferred
  from HTML/CSS to the geometry of OOXML shapes, with new thresholds.
  -> scripts/detect.py

SlideCraft's own material: the slide patterns and their evidence, the profiles and
their values, the deck plan format, the check script and its tests.
